    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d396">

                <pb facs="0721" n="706" xml:id="pg706"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">865.5043/9–2349: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Embassy in Italy
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-09-27T18:00:00-05:00">September 27,
                            1949—6 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2357. Fol is text of Thomas tel as recd in Dept, presumably same as qted in Mont.
                    art in <hi rendition="#italic">Umanità</hi> (urtel 2912 Sep 20<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d396-f1"/>): <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Have just recd from Ital news that the effort strongly supported by
                            Amers to force prematurely an artificial unity of autonomous trade
                            unions with the Catholic Federation does not further union but has
                            already created a new split among anti-totalitarian unionists and tends
                            to strengthen the large commie dominated federation. Since Amer
                            influence was behind effort to enforce premature union, I strongly urge
                            immed investigation by competent Amer experts of reasons for continuing
                            strength of commies largest Ital labor federation, the econ reasons for
                            the frequent strikes and the whole situation as affecting the struggle
                            against totalitarianism of the right or the left. Norman Thomas,
                            Chairman Post War World Council”<anchor n="2" xml:id="d396-f2"/>
                        </p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Since Thomas does not specifically request ans and his tel has recd no publicity
                    in US, Dept considers preferable let publicity in Ital die out rather than
                    stimulate it further with ans which wld surely find its way into Ital press
                    (urtel 2943 Sep 23<anchor n="3" xml:id="d396-f3"/>).</p>
                <p>In event of direct inquiries Rome, Emb may if it wishes state that of course no
                    US official attempting direct Ital labor developments, which US Govt regards as
                    Ital internal affairs.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d396-f1" n="1" xml:id="d396-f1-content">
                <p>In this telegram, not printed, Dunn reported that in an article which appeared in
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Umanità</hi>, Vanni Montana quoted a telegram
                    addressed by Norman Thomas to the Secretary of State requesting an investigation
                    whether American elements were responsible for Italian trade union discord.
                    (865.5043/9–2049)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d396-f2" n="2" xml:id="d396-f2-content">
                <p>Mr. Thomas’s telegram as received in the Department of State was dated September
                    14 at New York; the words abbreviated here were spelled out in full.
                    (865.5043/9–1449)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d396-f3" n="3" xml:id="d396-f3-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
